 "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLNumberOfLinesV","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberOfLines","text":"MXLNumberOfLines"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"lineThrough"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLNumberOfLinesV","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberOfLines","text":"MXLNumberOfLines"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"enclosure"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLEnclosureShapeO","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnclosureShape","text":"MXLEnclosureShape"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil)"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"id","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The optional-unique-id attribute group allows an element to optionally specify an ID"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that is unique to the entire document. This attribute group is not used for a required"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"id attribute, or for an id attribute that specifies an id reference."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One of the alternatives for Dynamics."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"items"},{"name":"position","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attributes let this be changed two ways."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"credit or direction. They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"font-family is a comma-separated list of font names. The font-style can be normal or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric point size. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"font vs. a music font."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"font"},{"name":"color","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In cases where text extends over more than one line, horizontal alignment and justify"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values can be different."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"halign"},{"name":"valign","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The valign attribute is used to indicate vertical alignment to the top, middle,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bottom, or baseline of the text. Defaults are implementation-dependent."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such as a note or a notation."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"placement"},{"name":"underline","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of lines used to underline the text: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":" (none), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"3"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of lines used to overline the text: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":" (none), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"3"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"overline"},{"name":"lineThrough","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of lines used to strike through the text: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":" (none), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"3"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The enclosure attribute group is used to specify the formatting of an enclosure around"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"text or symbols."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"enclosure"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldynamics\/init(id:items:position:font:color:halign:valign:placement:underline:overline:linethrough:enclosure:)"]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDynamics":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldynamics","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDynamics","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLDynamics","abstract":[{"text":"Dynamics can be associated either with a note or a general musical direction. To avoid inconsistencies between","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and among the letter abbreviations for dynamics (what is sf vs. sfz, standing alone or with a trailing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dynamic that is not always piano), we use the actual letters as the names of these dynamic elements. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other-dynamics element allows other dynamic marks that are not covered here. Dynamics elements may also be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"combined to create marks not covered by a single element, such as sfmp.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLDynamics","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPosition":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changed two ways."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlposition","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLPosition","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPosition"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPosition","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDynamics/Item":{"title":"MXLDynamics.Item","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldynamics\/item","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics\/Item","abstract":[{"text":"One of the alternatives for Dynamics.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLColor","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLValign":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLValign","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLValign","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The valign type is used to indicate vertical alignment to the top, middle, bottom, or baseline of the text. If"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the text is on multiple lines, baseline alignment refers to the baseline of the lowest line of text. Defaults"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are implementation-dependent."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLValign","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlvalign","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLValign","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAboveBelow":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLAboveBelow","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAboveBelow","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The above-below type is used to indicate whether one element appears above or below another element."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAboveBelow"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlabovebelow"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFont":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLFont","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFont","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"font names. The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is a text font"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vs. a music font."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLFont"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfont"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDynamics/init(id:items:position:font:color:halign:valign:placement:underline:overline:lineThrough:enclosure:)":{"title":"init(id:items:position:font:color:halign:valign:placement:underline:overline:lineThrough:enclosure:)","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"items"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLDynamicsV4ItemO","text":"Item"},{"kind":"text","text":"], "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"position"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLPositionV","text":"MXLPosition"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"font"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdent